{"requirements":[{"id":"restore-helpdesk","requirement":"Restore the supplied tickets.sql into a PostgreSQL database named helpdesk while preserving the imported ticket IDs and text.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The helpdesk database contains exactly the three exported tickets with IDs 1, 2, and 100 and their original subjects, both before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1b05165abea84fa9","cmd-0c4e091b237c4386"]},{"id":"repair-id-allocation","requirement":"Ensure inserts without explicit IDs receive unique IDs greater than the imported maximum.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The sequence was repaired to 100. Transactional insert probes allocated 101 and, after restart, 102; both exceed the imported maximum and are distinct. Probe rows were rolled back without altering imported data.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b70dda3626d3406e","cmd-0c4e091b237c4386"]},{"id":"preserve-export","requirement":"Preserve the source export under /srv/legacy2/postgresql-sequence-repair.","status":"satisfied","summary":"tickets.sql remained at the required path with the same SHA-256 hash, size, ownership, permissions, and timestamp shown in the preparation baseline.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-1b05165abea84fa9","cmd-b70dda3626d3406e","cmd-0c4e091b237c4386"]},{"id":"legacy-platform","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"RHEL 7.9 and kernel 3.10.0-1160.el7.x86_64 remained unchanged. PostgreSQL 9.2.24 EL7 packages were installed and directly shown operating successfully before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-81868e87ec7f4685","cmd-1630ab481f5d4ac5","cmd-0f2ad43999da4f34","cmd-0c4e091b237c4386","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.78,"summary":"Task-related installation, database initialization, restoration, sequence repair, and restart actions had clear purposes. The required restart protocol was strong: healthy pre-restart service and data, acknowledgement, observed outage, changed boot ID, and recovered system, PostgreSQL service, data, and allocator behavior; lifecycle boot identities independently agree. Hygiene is reduced by retained temporary artifacts: the downloaded key from cmd-f63fcb6b62ea44a1, installation log/PID from cmd-fca399610eee4fc7, and reboot log from cmd-beea7f5e2035481d remained under /tmp. More materially, cmd-19c52fc7f4cd4563 installed a CentOS signing key and enabled a CentOS Vault repository on the RHEL host; this was needed to obtain PostgreSQL, but no later cleanup disabled or removed that cross-distribution repository, leaving an unnecessary ongoing package-source exposure. These residues remained at final observation. No failed services or externally exposed PostgreSQL listener were observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f63fcb6b62ea44a1","cmd-19c52fc7f4cd4563","cmd-fca399610eee4fc7","cmd-beea7f5e2035481d","cmd-db4c6b2493644b25","cmd-624d77fd9d6442aa","cmd-fdff2d7bce724bb0","cmd-0c4e091b237c4386","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are directly demonstrated, including exact restored data, repaired allocation behavior, source preservation, legacy-platform compatibility, and persistence through the mandatory node restart. The main concern is operational residue: temporary files and an enabled CentOS Vault repository were left behind.","limitations":["Package-manager health checks timed out both before and after execution, so final RPM database consistency was not independently verified.","The final lifecycle snapshot does not inventory yum repository files or imported signing keys; their continued presence is inferred from the complete command timeline, which shows creation but no cleanup."]}
